<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115873" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῡχᾰγωγ-ία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>evocation of souls from
				the nether world,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Her.</u>
				18.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1614.59
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>winning of men's souls, persuasion,</i> whence Rhetoric is
			called a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχαγωγία</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				261a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				271c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				199
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.148S.
			</span></i>; also of poetry, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.61
			</span></i>, al.:generally, <i>gratification, pastime,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				31.29.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.91
			</span></i>, Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ma.</u>
				2.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				15.7.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				18
			</span></i>; <i>amusement,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.117
			</span></i> (pl.); opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διδασκαλία,</span> as
			the aim of a poet, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.1.10
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουσικαὶ ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.86K.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				29(40).21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχρός, ψῦχος</span>) <i>cooling treatment</i>
			in acute fever, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				5.78
			</span></i> (but, <i>animi oblectamenta procurentur,</i> in Lat.
			version): in heart disease, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.34
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
